1. What the equals method does by default?
compares if two object variables refer to the same object

2.In whihc class is the equals method defined?
In Object class.

3. How to actually use equals method for your purposes in inheritance tree?
override the equals method of Object class and modify it for your purposes

4. What checks should be implemented in equals method of subclass when you want to compare their state? (beside the state comparison)

check if two objects are identical (the same object)

check is the  reference passed as parameter is null

check if the object is of the same class

then the state check

5. How to guard yourself agains the possibility that the field might be null?

use Objects.equals(a,b)

6. what does the Objects.equals(a,b) method return?
it returns true if both are null, it returns false if one is null, it returns a.equals(b)  otherwise.

7. What  is required in equals method  of the subclass?
to first call for the equals method of superclass.

8. What the differences about equals method in records?
it is defined  automatically to compare its components.

9. How to compare components of type double in record? 
with Double.equals

